exports[`the quick estimate as the page is built 1`] = `"Quick estimate Enter your building's size and age, and untick any system it doesn't have. We price each one at typical costs. Rental units Year built Enter your units and year built to see an estimate. Already have quotes and install years? The full CapEx calculator uses your own numbers. Which systems does the building have? Typical installed costs in today's dollars, from the cost guides named under each one. A heat pump heats and cools, so untick central AC if heat pumps do the cooling. Systems and their typical replacement costs System Typical cost Lasts Roofing Asphalt shingle roof $2,600–$4,700 per apartment Based on 7,000 sq ft of roof × $4.50–$8, old shingles removed, ÷ 12 apartments Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 20–25 yrs Flat / membrane roof $3,000–$6,000 per apartment Based on 6,000 sq ft of roof × $6–$12, old roof removed, ÷ 12 apartments Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 15–25 yrs Gutters and downspouts $200–$400 per apartment Based on 480 ft of gutters and downspouts × $5–$10, including $1 a foot to take the old ones down (our estimate), ÷ 12 apartments Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 20–30 yrs HVAC Gas furnace $2,500–$5,000 per apartment Based on one small furnace for each apartment Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 15–20 yrs Central AC / condenser $3,500–$6,500 per apartment Based on one 2-ton system for each apartment Source: This Old House (opens in a new tab) 12–15 yrs Heat pump $4,000–$7,000 per apartment Based on one 2-ton system for each apartment, indoor unit included Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 12–15 yrs Boiler $1,100–$2,900 per apartment Based on one 300,000–600,000 BTU boiler at $13,000–$35,000, ÷ 12 apartments Source: OxMaint (opens in a new tab) 20–30 yrs Plumbing Tank water heater $800–$2,300 per apartment Based on one 40-gallon heater for each apartment Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 8–12 yrs Tankless water heater $1,400–$3,900 per apartment Based on one for each apartment Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 15–20 yrs Appliances Refrigerator $700–$1,300 per apartment Based on a basic 18 cu ft top-freezer at $500–$1,000, plus $200–$300 to install Sources: Fixr (opens in a new tab) , HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 10–15 yrs Range / oven $600–$1,300 per apartment Based on a basic freestanding range at $500–$1,000, plus $100–$300 to install Source: HomeServe (opens in a new tab) 13–15 yrs Dishwasher $500–$1,100 per apartment Based on a basic dishwasher, installed Source: Bob Vila (opens in a new tab) 9–12 yrs Washer / dryer $900–$2,000 per apartment Based on a basic top-load washer and dryer, installed Source: Fixr (opens in a new tab) 10–13 yrs Flooring Carpet $3–$6 per sq ft, 800 sq ft per apartment Based on rental-grade carpet and pad, old carpet removed Source: NerdWallet (opens in a new tab) 5–10 yrs Luxury vinyl plank $4–$8 per sq ft, 800 sq ft per apartment Based on floating plank, plus $1–$2 per sq ft to remove the old floor Source: Bob Vila (opens in a new tab) 15–25 yrs Interior Interior paint (turnover) $1,800–$3,600 per apartment Based on a 900 sq ft apartment × $2–$4, one standard color Source: Lula (opens in a new tab) 3–7 yrs Kitchen cabinets $2,000–$6,000 per apartment Based on 20 ft of stock cabinets × $100–$300 per ft Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 20–30 yrs Laminate countertops $500–$1,500 per apartment Based on 30 sq ft × $15–$40, plus $50–$300 to remove the old top Source: Fixr (opens in a new tab) 15–20 yrs Exterior Windows (vinyl) $3,200–$7,200 per apartment Based on 8 windows × $400–$900 Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 20–30 yrs Exterior paint $900–$2,800 per apartment Based on 5,500 sq ft of wall × $2–$6, ÷ 12 apartments Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 7–10 yrs Vinyl siding $1,600–$3,200 per apartment Based on 5,500 sq ft of wall × $3.50–$7, old siding removed, ÷ 12 apartments Source: NerdWallet (opens in a new tab) 20–40 yrs Site Parking lot seal coat $0.15–$0.30 per sq ft, 500 sq ft per apartment Sources: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) , SealMaster (opens in a new tab) 3–5 yrs Parking lot resurface $2–$4 per sq ft, 500 sq ft per apartment Based on our estimate for an overlay, which costs less than the $2.50–$4.50 for new paving Source: HomeAdvisor (opens in a new tab) 15–20 yrs Electrical Electrical panel $1,000–$2,500 per apartment Based on one 100 amp panel for each apartment Source: NerdWallet (opens in a new tab) 25–40 yrs Safety Fire alarm panel $250–$850 per apartment Based on a $1,500–$8,000 panel, plus $1,500–$2,000 to install and program it (our estimate), ÷ 12 apartments Source: 2M Technology (opens in a new tab) 15–20 yrs How the estimate works Each system you tick has been replaced on schedule since the building was built. No two last exactly the same time, so each one's life is spread across its typical lifespan, and each replacement can land up to 2 years early or late. Those add up over the years, so the older the building, the more evenly each system's next replacement is spread over the years ahead. Nothing is overdue. The monthly amount is worked out like the full calculator's: the smallest steady amount, starting from nothing saved, that has the cash ready for every replacement after this year, looking 30 years ahead. A system due in the next year or two raises it a lot. The low figure uses every low cost, and the high figure every high cost. No inflation. Costs for the whole building, like the roof, are shared out per apartment for a 12-unit, two-story building. A bigger building usually costs less per apartment, and a smaller one more. Carpet and vinyl plank cover 800 sq ft per apartment: a 900 sq ft apartment ( RentCafe (opens in a new tab) ) less its kitchen and bathroom. Parking is 500 sq ft per apartment: 1.5 spaces ( Sightline Institute (opens in a new tab) ) of about 325 sq ft each, driving lanes included ( Hunker (opens in a new tab) ). If you tick more than one kind of roof, heating, water heater or floor, each covers an equal share."`;

exports[`the replace-now comparison on the example building, 0% emergency premium 1`] = `"If you replace all 4 items below in 2026: If you replace the 4 ticked items in 2026: Tick at least one item below to compare. Cash needed in 2026 $70,400 $30,000 if you wait 10-year total $38,400 more $201,200, or $162,800 if you wait Monthly reserve $1,884 $2,684 if you wait $157 per unit, or $224 if you wait The monthly amount is lower because these are paid now instead of saved for. The monthly amount stays the same. The monthly amount is higher. Items past end of life or due in 2026 are paid in 2026 either way, so the difference comes from items due in the next 2 years. Items past end of life or due in 2026 are paid in 2026 either way, so the difference comes from items due in the next 2 years and the emergency extra. Emergency replacements cost % more Optional. Use it if waiting until something breaks costs more, such as rush fees or water damage. Here, waiting costs 25% more for each item's next replacement. The forecast above doesn't include it. Enter a percent from 0 to 500, like 25. Replace in 2026 Tank water heater Due 2026. $16,800 Parking lot seal coat Due 2027. $2,000 Carpet Due 2028. $38,400 Check these install years before applying. Refrigerator Past due since 2011. No install year, so year built (1998) is used. $13,200 Apply to 4 items Apply ticks Replace this year for the items you chose. Nothing changes until you click it."`;

exports[`the replace-now comparison on the example building, 25% emergency premium 1`] = `"If you replace all 4 items below in 2026: If you replace the 4 ticked items in 2026: Tick at least one item below to compare. Cash needed in 2026 $70,400 $37,500 if you wait 10-year total $20,800 more $201,200, or $180,400 if you wait Monthly reserve $1,884 $2,894 if you wait $157 per unit, or $242 if you wait The monthly amount is lower because these are paid now instead of saved for. The monthly amount stays the same. The monthly amount is higher. Items past end of life or due in 2026 are paid in 2026 either way, so the difference comes from items due in the next 2 years. Items past end of life or due in 2026 are paid in 2026 either way, so the difference comes from items due in the next 2 years and the emergency extra. Emergency replacements cost % more Optional. Use it if waiting until something breaks costs more, such as rush fees or water damage. Here, waiting costs 25% more for each item's next replacement. The forecast above doesn't include it. Enter a percent from 0 to 500, like 25. Replace in 2026 Tank water heater Due 2026. $16,800 Parking lot seal coat Due 2027. $2,000 Carpet Due 2028. $38,400 Check these install years before applying. Refrigerator Past due since 2011. No install year, so year built (1998) is used. $13,200 Apply to 4 items Apply ticks Replace this year for the items you chose. Nothing changes until you click it."`;

exports[`the sample condition report in 2026 1`] = `"CAPEXCLOCK · CONDITION REPORT SAMPLE 12-unit apartment building 12 units · built 1998 · prepared October 1, 2026 Prepared by CapexClock from information the owner supplied. A planning document, not an inspection. This is a sample. It uses the CapexClock calculator's example building, and the building, conditions and notes are made up. Summary Monthly reserve $2,684 Per unit, per month $224 Needed in 2026 $30,000 10-year total $162,800 The monthly reserve is the smallest steady amount that has the cash ready for every replacement from 2027 on, looking 30 years ahead. 2026 costs (past end of life or due this year) are shown separately as needed now. All costs are in today's dollars, without inflation. Property Units 12 units Year built 1998 Components listed 6 Condition, rated by the owner 2 good, 3 fair, 1 poor At risk 4 of 6 (past end of life or due within 2 years) Information supplied by The owner, October 2026 At risk • Refrigerator : 15 years past its end of life (2011), condition fair. Install year estimated. Replacement $13,200. • Tank water heater : due this year (2026), condition fair. Replacement $16,800. • Parking lot seal coat : due in 1 year (2027), condition good. Replacement $2,000. • Carpet : due in 2 years (2028), condition poor. Replacement $38,400. Prepared by CapexClock from information the owner supplied. A planning document, not an inspection. CAPEXCLOCK · CONDITION REPORT SAMPLE Components Component Qty Installed Age Life Remaining Condition Replacement Refrigerator Appliances Past end of life 12 1998* 28 years (est.) 13 yrs 15 years past Fair $13,200 Owner's notes: Replaced one at a time over the years; install dates weren't kept. Tank water heater Plumbing Due within 2 years 12 2016 10 years 10 yrs Due this year Fair $16,800 Owner's notes: Rust at the fittings in units 3 and 7. Parking lot seal coat Site Due within 2 years 8,000 sq ft 2023 3 years 4 yrs 1 year Good $2,000 Owner's notes: Cracks filled in 2025. Carpet Flooring Due within 2 years 9,600 sq ft 2020 6 years 8 yrs 2 years Poor $38,400 Owner's notes: Worn through in the hallways of units 2, 5 and 9. Asphalt shingle roof Roofing 1 2008 18 years 22 yrs 4 years Fair $38,000 Owner's notes: Some granule loss on the south slope. No leaks reported. Gas furnace HVAC 12 2012 14 years 18 yrs 4 years Good $50,400 Owner's notes: Serviced every fall. No repairs in the last two years. Age and remaining life are counted from the install year to 2026. Life is the useful life the owner chose. Remaining life is the install year plus the useful life, minus 2026. At risk means past end of life or due within 2 years. Replacement is the quantity times the owner's cost each, in today's dollars. * No install year was recorded for refrigerator, so the year built is used, and the age is an estimate. Prepared by CapexClock from information the owner supplied. A planning document, not an inspection. CAPEXCLOCK · CONDITION REPORT SAMPLE 10-year forecast, 2026–2035 2026 [bar 33.93665158371041%] $30,000 2027 [bar 2.262443438914027%] $2,000 2028 [bar 43.43891402714932%] $38,400 2029 $0 2030 [bar 100%] $88,400 2031 [bar 2.262443438914027%] $2,000 2032 $0 2033 $0 2034 $0 2035 [bar 2.262443438914027%] $2,000 What's due when Year Component Note Cost 2026 Tank water heater $16,800 2026 Refrigerator Overdue; Install year estimated $13,200 2027 Parking lot seal coat $2,000 2028 Carpet $38,400 2030 Asphalt shingle roof $38,000 2030 Gas furnace $50,400 2031 Parking lot seal coat $2,000 2035 Parking lot seal coat $2,000 About this report Prepared by CapexClock from information the owner supplied. A planning document, not an inspection. We didn't visit or inspect the building. The install years, quantities, useful lives, costs, conditions and notes are the owner's, as of October 2026, and the report is only as accurate as they are. The owner may share this report with anyone, such as a lender or a buyer. No one but the owner may rely on it, and buyers and lenders should get their own inspection. Anything to do with safety, such as gas, electrical, structure or water damage, needs a licensed professional. This report never says a system is safe. Questions: support@capexclock.com · capexclock.com Prepared by CapexClock from information the owner supplied. A planning document, not an inspection."`;
